summary: Check that Kernel-Address-Sanitizer (KASAN) is enabled.
description: |
    a read-after-free error in the kernels memory space, and then searches "dmesg"
    for the resulting error message.  KASAN is currently only enabled on:
     * RHEL-8,
     * Debug kernels,
     * x86_64 & aarch64 architectures.

    Author: David McDougall <dmcdouga@redhat.com>
contact: David McDougall <dmcdouga@redhat.com>
component:
  - kernel-debug
test: bash ./runtest.sh
id: 126bb37b-17f2-44a4-bff3-d7e4aa3b6195
framework: beakerlib
duration: 30m
extra-summary: /kernel/general/memory/function/kasan
extra-task: /kernel/general/memory/function/kasan

